#!/bin/sh
# Taskwarrior on-modify hook: keeps the `cerebro' tag in sync if a
# task's project is changed into or out of `academic'/`academic.*'
# after creation (on-add alone would miss that case).
#
# Installed via `make install-hooks' (symlinked into ~/.task/hooks/);
# canonical copy lives here, versioned with everything else.
#
# Protocol (Taskwarrior hook API): two lines on stdin, old task JSON
# then new task JSON; print the (possibly modified) new task JSON as
# the first line of stdout.
set -eu

IFS= read -r old_json
IFS= read -r new_json

project=$(printf '%s' "$new_json" | jq -r '.project // empty')

case "$project" in
    academic|academic.*)
        new_json=$(printf '%s' "$new_json" | jq -c '
            .tags = ((.tags // []) + ["cerebro"] | unique)
        ')
        ;;
    *)
        new_json=$(printf '%s' "$new_json" | jq -c '
            .tags = ((.tags // []) - ["cerebro"])
        ')
        ;;
esac

printf '%s\n' "$new_json"
